url: "https://piotrspychalski.github.io/surgitome/"
abstract: >-
  SURGITOME is an interactive, schematic 3D atlas of anatomy after gastrointestinal surgery.
  For 29 operations in oesophageal, gastric, bariatric, hepatopancreatobiliary, liver,
  small-bowel and colorectal surgery (57 variants) it shows the extent of resection, the
  reconstruction and anastomoses, the postoperative endoscopic view and schematic CT sections.
  The interface is in Polish and English. It is intended for surgical education and for
  communication with patients. The source code is released under the MIT License; the content
  (3D anatomical models, illustrations and texts) under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-CONTENT).
  SURGITOME is a schematic educational tool, not a medical device.
keywords:
  - postoperative anatomy
  - surgical education
  - 3D atlas
  - colorectal surgery
  - gastrointestinal surgery
  - patient education
